  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Universal property of the scheme-theoretic image",
  "statement": "The composite of $g^{\\mathrm{im}}$ with\n$\\operatorname{SIm}(g)\\hookrightarrow Y$ is $g$. For every closed\nfactorization through $Z$, the constructed map $c_{g,Z}$ is a closed\nimmersion compatible with the maps to $Y$, and it is the unique compatible\nmorphism $\\operatorname{SIm}(g)\\to Z$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-closure/lemma-nagata-scheme-image-universal.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-scheme-image-universal, order 71"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-nagata-scheme-image-comparison",
    "def-nagata-scheme-image-factor",
    "def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-closure",
    "def-nagata-scheme-theoretic-image"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "The factorization equality is `Scheme.Hom.toImage_imageι`.\nLet $\\mathcal I_Z$ be the ideal of $Z$. From\n$z\\circ h=g$ every local section of $\\mathcal I_Z$ maps to zero under $g$,\nso $\\mathcal I_Z\\subseteq\\operatorname{ker}(g)$. The induced quotient map\ntherefore gives a closed immersion\n$c_{g,Z}\\colon\\operatorname{SIm}(g)\\to Z$; its composite with $z$ is the\nimage inclusion by construction. If $c'$ is another compatible map, then\ncomposing both $c'$ and $c_{g,Z}$ with the closed immersion $z$ gives the\nsame image inclusion\n\n$$\nz\\circ c'=g_{\\mathrm{im}}=z\\circ c_{g,Z}.\n$$",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    },
    {
      "text": "A closed immersion is a monomorphism, so cancellation of $z$ gives\n$c'=c_{g,Z}$.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
